WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.160
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.430 --> 01:34.920
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.280 --> 01:37.670
[Episode 40]

4
01:38.789 --> 01:39.590
Comrades,

5
01:39.950 --> 01:43.229
on behalf of the Central Politburo, I hereby announce the new appointments:

6
01:43.229 --> 01:45.150
Comrade Xu Xiangqian,

7
01:45.430 --> 01:48.229
Chen Changhao, and Zhou Chunquan are appointed as

8
01:48.229 --> 01:49.509
members of the Central Committee.

9
01:49.509 --> 01:53.229
Chen Changhao and Zhou Chunquan are

10
01:53.509 --> 01:54.710
appointed as members of the Politburo.

11
01:54.710 --> 01:57.380
The addition of Comrades He Wei, Li Xiannian,

12
01:57.380 --> 01:58.710
and Fu Zhong are appointed as

13
01:58.710 --> 02:01.240
alternate members of the Central Committee.

14
02:16.630 --> 02:17.579
I think

15
02:18.360 --> 02:20.560
as the Workers' and Peasants' Red Army,

16
02:21.530 --> 02:23.230
we must promote more cadres

17
02:23.310 --> 02:24.980
from working-class and peasant backgrounds

18
02:24.980 --> 02:26.260
into the Politburo.

19
02:27.030 --> 02:28.560
And this is very necessary.

20
02:42.950 --> 02:44.390
According to the Party Constitution,

21
02:44.390 --> 02:46.380
the Politburo does not have the authority

22
02:46.380 --> 02:48.310
to decide who becomes a member of the Central Committee.

23
02:48.310 --> 02:51.510
We're only doing this today because of the special circumstances.

24
02:51.510 --> 02:53.579
The comrades just appointed

25
02:53.790 --> 02:54.910
already represent

26
02:54.910 --> 02:56.710
the cadres of the 4th Front Army.

27
02:57.160 --> 02:58.070
When the opportunity comes,

28
02:58.070 --> 02:59.670
we can promote more comrades

29
02:59.700 --> 03:03.510
to other leadership positions.

30
03:03.970 --> 03:06.570
Not everyone needs to be on the Central Committee.

31
03:06.570 --> 03:07.430
Comrade Luofu,

32
03:08.690 --> 03:09.970
I have a suggestion.

33
03:10.660 --> 03:11.230
Go ahead.

34
03:14.190 --> 03:15.590
I suggest that we restore

35
03:15.860 --> 03:18.470
the headquarters of the 1st Front Army

36
03:18.950 --> 03:22.140
and make some adjustments to the command structure.

37
03:22.820 --> 03:24.750
I recommend Comrade Zhou Enlai

38
03:24.910 --> 03:27.070
to serve concurrently as Commander

39
03:27.420 --> 03:30.020
and Political Commissar of the 1st Front Army.

40
03:30.140 --> 03:31.540
I agree with Mao's proposal.

41
03:31.540 --> 03:31.950
Agreed.

42
03:31.950 --> 03:32.550
Agreed.

43
03:32.570 --> 03:33.640
I agree too.

44
03:40.790 --> 03:41.950
Comrade Enlai,

45
03:43.260 --> 03:45.790
you need to get well as soon as possible.

46
03:47.960 --> 03:50.620
The 1st Front Army still needs your leadership.

47
03:50.800 --> 03:51.920
Otherwise,

48
03:52.420 --> 03:56.579
we can't let the commander-in-chief become

49
03:56.650 --> 03:58.850
as thin as the commanders and fighters.

50
03:59.940 --> 04:00.610
Yes.

51
04:01.190 --> 04:04.590
The 1st Front Army soldiers marched all the way from Jiangxi,

52
04:04.630 --> 04:07.490
and they've certainly grown thinner along the way.

53
04:07.580 --> 04:08.750
Just like me,

54
04:09.310 --> 04:10.570
I'm skin and bones now.

55
04:11.310 --> 04:14.140
But you, Comrade Guotao,

56
04:14.380 --> 04:16.430
are still strong and well-fed.

57
04:16.779 --> 04:19.060
You should help us more in the future.

58
04:19.140 --> 04:20.800
That's what comrades are for.

59
04:30.260 --> 04:31.140
Definitely.

60
04:33.190 --> 04:35.120
May we all stay strong and healthy.

61
04:35.330 --> 04:36.790
We should all stay strong.

62
04:37.150 --> 04:38.680
Everyone should be strong.

63
04:58.950 --> 04:59.820
Chairman Zhang.

64
04:59.820 --> 05:00.420
Changhao.

65
05:00.560 --> 05:01.990
Hurry, I just heated it up.

66
05:01.990 --> 05:02.950
Eat it while it's hot.

67
05:02.950 --> 05:04.880
You must be tired from the meeting.

68
05:09.570 --> 05:11.530
Changhao, how did the meeting go?

69
05:11.820 --> 05:13.990
The Central Committee didn't listen to Chairman Zhang at all.

70
05:13.990 --> 05:15.380
They insist on moving north

71
05:15.380 --> 05:17.840
and carrying out the Xia-Tao Campaign Plan.

72
05:19.380 --> 05:20.670
Personally, I think,

73
05:20.690 --> 05:22.090
given the current situation,

74
05:22.090 --> 05:24.420
although moving north will be difficult,

75
05:24.750 --> 05:27.020
the overall direction is still correct.

76
05:27.240 --> 05:28.700
We should proceed with it.

77
05:29.120 --> 05:31.450
Xiangqian, about your current stance...

78
05:31.500 --> 05:32.110
I think...

79
05:32.140 --> 05:34.070
Changhao, don't interrupt.

80
05:34.900 --> 05:36.380
Go on, Xiangqian.

81
05:45.630 --> 05:47.890
Chairman Zhang, I wasn't at the meeting,

82
05:48.070 --> 05:49.580
so I don't know the details of the disagreements

83
05:49.580 --> 05:51.640
and what the disagreement was about.

84
05:52.020 --> 05:52.870
All I know is

85
05:53.140 --> 05:55.140
that our troops are stationed here,

86
05:56.510 --> 05:57.710
and we're out of food.

87
05:58.780 --> 06:01.990
So many soldiers are eating jute leaves and wild herbs

88
06:02.220 --> 06:03.780
that their mouths are swelling up.

89
06:03.780 --> 06:05.310
A perfectly healthy sol...

90
06:06.880 --> 06:08.470
A perfectly healthy soldier can be marching along,

91
06:08.470 --> 06:09.950
then suddenly collapse and

92
06:09.950 --> 06:11.190
never get back up.

93
06:11.750 --> 06:13.350
Vice Chairman Zhou is so ill.

94
06:13.550 --> 06:14.750
I wanted to visit him,

95
06:14.980 --> 06:17.410
but it was so hard to find anything to bring him.

96
06:17.410 --> 06:18.330
No matter what,

97
06:18.820 --> 06:20.670
we can't afford any more non-combat casualties.

98
06:20.670 --> 06:22.510
It's normal for you

99
06:22.990 --> 06:24.220
to disagree and argue.

100
06:24.220 --> 06:26.020
Why don't we find somewhere to get food first,

101
06:26.020 --> 06:27.880
then sit down and work things out?

102
06:33.940 --> 06:35.070
Drink it while it's hot.

103
06:35.070 --> 06:36.930
With such a shortage of supplies,

104
06:37.980 --> 06:39.710
where did you get this milk tea?

105
06:54.460 --> 06:56.450
Xiangqian, I think you make a good point.

106
06:56.450 --> 06:58.050
I'll return to Zhuokeji now.

107
06:58.080 --> 07:00.050
Once I meet up with Comrade Zhu De,

108
07:01.030 --> 07:03.000
I'll lead the Left Route Army north.

109
07:03.000 --> 07:06.680
You and Changhao will be responsible for the Right Route Army.

110
07:08.780 --> 07:09.290
Okay.

111
07:10.110 --> 07:11.010
Then I'll go check how the troops

112
07:11.010 --> 07:12.900
are managing their food supplies.

113
07:12.900 --> 07:13.630
Eat quickly.

114
07:19.540 --> 07:20.470
Chairman Zhang.

115
07:21.020 --> 07:21.950
Lately,

116
07:22.700 --> 07:23.630
has Comrade Xiangqian seemed a little...

117
07:23.630 --> 07:25.360
I know what you're going to say.

118
07:26.260 --> 07:28.590
That medal he received at Upper Luhua

119
07:28.820 --> 07:30.430
must have meant a lot to him.

120
07:31.720 --> 07:33.370
He really took it to heart.

121
07:39.340 --> 07:40.550
But no matter what,

122
07:40.920 --> 07:43.420
the 4th Front Army must stay united.

123
07:44.150 --> 07:45.880
We must think as one

124
07:46.210 --> 07:49.330
and work together.

125
07:49.950 --> 07:50.630
Yes.

126
07:55.710 --> 07:56.640
There's no salt.

127
07:57.920 --> 07:59.560
I forgot. I'll go get some.

128
08:03.350 --> 08:04.550
Forget it. Forget it.

129
08:48.400 --> 08:51.890
Comrade Keqing, take this highland barley.

130
08:52.170 --> 08:54.270
Eat it with the Commander-in-Chief on the way.

131
08:54.270 --> 08:56.100
This is too precious. Keep it for yourself.

132
08:54.620 --> 08:57.190
[Kang Keqing, Zhu De's wife]

133
08:56.190 --> 08:56.980
Just take it.

134
09:05.030 --> 09:08.270
Comrade Keqing, take this bag of salt.

135
09:12.670 --> 09:13.470
Go on, take it.

136
09:16.550 --> 09:18.760
Take this beef for the journey.

137
09:18.790 --> 09:20.950
Comrade Enlai, I really can't take the beef.

138
09:20.950 --> 09:22.190
I heard from Xiaochao

139
09:22.430 --> 09:25.070
that Xu Xiangqian prepared it for you because you're ill.

140
09:25.070 --> 09:26.930
But you gave it all away to others.

141
09:27.430 --> 09:29.090
It's the thought that counts.

142
09:29.340 --> 09:31.730
But you're clearly in worse shape than we are.

143
09:31.730 --> 09:33.530
Every cloud has a silver lining.

144
09:50.320 --> 09:53.030
Vice Chairman Zhou, take care of yourself.

145
09:53.210 --> 09:53.810
Take care.

146
09:53.860 --> 09:54.620
Take care.

147
09:59.100 --> 10:01.340
Commander-in-Chief, Comrade Bocheng,

148
10:01.340 --> 10:03.310
when you reach the Left Route Army,

149
10:03.670 --> 10:05.000
take care of yourselves

150
10:05.740 --> 10:06.700
and stay safe.

151
10:07.500 --> 10:08.150
Okay.

152
10:08.340 --> 10:09.150
Don't worry.

153
10:10.620 --> 10:13.550
We've made it through such a difficult journey.

154
10:14.190 --> 10:16.910
I've been toughened by years of hardship.

155
10:17.620 --> 10:19.450
The conflict between Zhang Guotao and the Central Committee

156
10:19.450 --> 10:21.220
has not been completely resolved.

157
10:21.220 --> 10:23.620
With you and Comrade Bocheng joining the Left Route Army,

158
10:23.620 --> 10:26.150
we are still a little worried.

159
10:26.570 --> 10:28.860
It's a concern shared by all of us.

160
10:29.100 --> 10:29.830
Don't worry.

161
10:30.220 --> 10:32.740
No matter how domineering Zhang Guotao is,

162
10:32.900 --> 10:34.030
he can't change the fact

163
10:34.030 --> 10:36.830
that the Red Army is under the Party's leadership.

164
10:37.910 --> 10:40.040
If anyone dares to split the Red Army

165
10:40.070 --> 10:41.200
or divide the Party,

166
10:41.700 --> 10:43.910
Bocheng and I will fight them to the end.

167
10:44.820 --> 10:45.980
I'd like to see

168
10:46.050 --> 10:47.740
what he thinks he can do to me,

169
10:47.910 --> 10:48.980
the Commander-in-Chief of the Red Army.

170
10:48.980 --> 10:51.070
Rest assured, comrades of the Central Committee and the Military Commission.

171
10:51.070 --> 10:54.070
We will always follow the CPC Central Committee.

172
10:55.030 --> 10:56.980
Following the lead of the CPC Central Committee

173
10:56.980 --> 10:59.440
means standing on the right side of history.

174
11:18.100 --> 11:20.460
Old friend, we'll be apart for a while.

175
11:22.220 --> 11:22.880
Changfeng.

176
11:22.910 --> 11:23.500
Here.

177
11:25.540 --> 11:26.870
Give me that cigarette.

178
11:32.030 --> 11:32.820
Not this one.

179
11:33.550 --> 11:34.310
Not this one?

180
11:34.820 --> 11:35.880
It's the cigarette I asked you to keep for me

181
11:35.880 --> 11:38.150
after our first crossing of the Chishui River.

182
11:38.150 --> 11:40.310
The first crossing of the Chishui River?

183
11:40.310 --> 11:41.840
I specifically told you...

184
11:44.100 --> 11:44.670
Mao.

185
11:46.310 --> 11:48.620
The bullets at Qinggangpo couldn't hit me,

186
11:48.620 --> 11:51.150
and Zhang Guotao won't dare touch me, either.

187
11:51.670 --> 11:53.070
Zhu and Mao will never be separated.

188
11:53.070 --> 11:54.400
A temporary separation

189
11:54.760 --> 11:57.090
will only make our reunion all the better.

190
12:34.180 --> 12:35.820
Chairman, I remember now.

191
13:27.220 --> 13:28.020
Chairman Mao.

192
13:29.740 --> 13:31.200
Greetings, Chairman Mao.

193
13:31.220 --> 13:32.100
Welcome.

194
13:32.790 --> 13:33.590
Chairman Mao.

195
13:33.790 --> 13:35.140
Let me introduce everyone.

196
13:35.140 --> 13:36.500
These are the commanders of the Fourth Red Army

197
13:36.500 --> 13:38.260
and the Thirtieth Red Army.

198
13:38.500 --> 13:40.360
You've met Comrade Xiannian before.

199
13:40.360 --> 13:41.200
[Li Xiannian, Political Commissar of the 30th Red Army]

200
13:40.460 --> 13:41.430
Hello, Chairman.

201
13:41.430 --> 13:43.190
This is the Acting Commander of the Thirtieth Red Army...

202
13:43.190 --> 13:44.190
Comrade Cheng Shicai.

203
13:44.190 --> 13:44.620
Yes.

204
13:44.820 --> 13:46.000
I recognized you at a glance.

205
13:46.000 --> 13:47.620
[Cheng Shicai, Acting Commander of the 30th Red Army]

206
13:46.270 --> 13:47.820
You always carry that long rifle.

207
13:47.820 --> 13:50.020
and are the first to charge into battle.

208
13:50.220 --> 13:51.670
Hello, Comrade Cheng Shicai.

209
13:51.670 --> 13:52.070
Greetings, Chairman Mao.

210
13:52.070 --> 13:52.600
Welcome.

211
13:53.000 --> 13:53.700
He's the Fourth Red Army's...

212
13:53.700 --> 13:54.740
Comrade Wang Jian'an.

213
13:54.740 --> 13:55.190
Yes.

214
13:55.620 --> 13:56.860
Greetings, Chairman.

215
13:56.860 --> 13:58.790
You and Comrade Li Xiannian are from the same hometown, right?

216
13:57.960 --> 13:59.870
[Wang Jian'an, Political Commissar of the Fourth Red Army]

217
13:58.980 --> 13:59.430
Yes.

218
13:59.830 --> 14:00.620
Welcome, Comrade Jian'an.

219
14:00.620 --> 14:01.820
Thank you, Chairman.

220
14:02.270 --> 14:02.950
Greetings, Chairman Mao.

221
14:02.840 --> 14:04.850
[Xu Shiyu, Commander of the Fourth Red Army]

222
14:03.220 --> 14:05.310
I'm Xu Shiyou, Commander of the Fourth Red Army.

223
14:05.310 --> 14:06.030
Xu Shiyou.

224
14:06.620 --> 14:07.890
I've heard a lot about you.

225
14:07.890 --> 14:09.190
During the Counter-Encirclement Campaign in Hubei-Henan-Anhui,

226
14:09.190 --> 14:10.740
you joined the dare-to-die squad seven times.

227
14:10.740 --> 14:12.150
You were absolutely fearless.

228
14:12.150 --> 14:13.550
You even know about that?

229
14:13.610 --> 14:15.940
Of course. Your reputation precedes you.

230
14:16.580 --> 14:19.220
Which three Chinese characters are used to write your name, Xu Shiyou?

231
14:19.220 --> 14:20.700
Chairman, I...

232
14:21.910 --> 14:24.910
My surname "Xu" consists of "yan" (speech) and "wu" (noon).

233
14:24.910 --> 14:26.880
And I'm from the "Shi" generation of my family,

234
14:26.880 --> 14:28.680
so my parents named me Xu Shiyou.

235
14:29.070 --> 14:30.030
It was only after I joined the Red Army

236
14:30.030 --> 14:32.100
that I learned the "Shi" meant "official."

237
14:32.100 --> 14:32.900
So I changed it

238
14:33.030 --> 14:34.430
to the character meaning "soldier."

239
14:34.430 --> 14:36.560
So my name means "friend of soldiers."

240
14:36.730 --> 14:38.390
A true friend of the soldiers!

241
14:38.430 --> 14:39.310
How about I

242
14:39.910 --> 14:41.840
change one character in your name?

243
14:48.980 --> 14:50.290
Let's use the "Shi" for "world" instead.

244
14:50.290 --> 14:51.950
We need to look farther ahead.

245
14:52.270 --> 14:53.380
We're heading north to fight the Japanese;

246
14:53.380 --> 14:54.550
we must think beyond our borders.

247
14:54.550 --> 14:55.890
This way, your name Xu Shiyou

248
14:55.890 --> 14:57.390
means a friend of the world.

249
14:57.390 --> 14:58.150
This is good.

250
14:58.340 --> 14:59.310
This character has a much broader meaning.

251
14:59.310 --> 15:01.030
From now on, I'll use this character.

252
15:01.030 --> 15:02.690
Then I'm a friend of the world!

253
15:04.030 --> 15:04.830
Chairman Mao.

254
15:06.500 --> 15:07.660
We have a new intelligence report.

255
15:07.660 --> 15:11.380
[Ye Jianying, Chief of Staff Red Army Frontline General Headquarters]

256
15:07.930 --> 15:09.110
The troops of Liu Wenhui and Li Baobing

257
15:09.110 --> 15:10.270
suddenly launched an attack.

258
15:10.270 --> 15:12.400
Dangba and Gengda Bridge have fallen.

259
15:13.190 --> 15:14.070
At the same time,

260
15:14.070 --> 15:15.460
the troops of Hu Zongnan and Xue Yue

261
15:15.460 --> 15:16.910
have also started mobilizing forces,

262
15:16.910 --> 15:18.710
putting further pressure on us.

263
15:21.100 --> 15:22.070
The enemy situation has changed.

264
15:22.070 --> 15:22.650
Just in time.

265
15:22.650 --> 15:24.220
Let's go to Enlai's quarters

266
15:24.220 --> 15:25.620
and discuss it together.

267
15:25.820 --> 15:26.190
Yes, Chairman.

268
15:26.190 --> 15:26.720
Let's go.

269
15:36.150 --> 15:37.280
From what we can see,

270
15:38.580 --> 15:40.880
the enemy may have figured out

271
15:41.100 --> 15:43.540
that we intend to head north through Xiahe and Taohe.

272
15:43.540 --> 15:45.340
Our troops need to move quickly.

273
15:46.460 --> 15:47.100
Enlai,

274
15:47.820 --> 15:49.910
your opinion aligns with ours.

275
15:50.340 --> 15:51.700
I have discussed it with Comrade Changhao

276
15:51.700 --> 15:53.310
and Comrade Xiangqian.

277
15:53.860 --> 15:54.590
In that case,

278
15:54.950 --> 15:57.270
we will change our previous deployment

279
15:57.380 --> 15:59.650
of the Left Route Army attacking Aba,

280
16:00.190 --> 16:02.550
and order it to move quickly toward us instead.

281
16:02.550 --> 16:04.950
Both armies will cross the grasslands at the same time

282
16:04.950 --> 16:06.350
and head north to Banyou.

283
16:06.910 --> 16:09.340
We'd like to hear your thoughts on this.

284
16:10.070 --> 16:12.200
I completely agree with your opinion.

285
16:12.270 --> 16:13.470
ur most urgent task is

286
16:13.550 --> 16:15.500
for the Left Route Army to act immediately

287
16:15.500 --> 16:17.860
and head north to join us as soon as possible.

288
16:17.860 --> 16:18.500
Okay.

289
16:19.340 --> 16:20.800
Since we are in agreement,

290
16:21.390 --> 16:23.620
let's send a telegram in the name of the Central Revolutionary Military Commission

291
16:23.620 --> 16:26.500
to Comrade Zhang Guotao and Comrade Zhu De,

292
16:26.740 --> 16:28.500
asking them to take the new route

293
16:28.500 --> 16:29.760
and move north at once.

294
16:30.790 --> 16:31.270
Okay.

295
16:32.960 --> 16:40.090
[Zhuokeji, Lifan County, Sichuan]

296
16:51.700 --> 16:52.500
Comrade Guotao.

297
16:52.500 --> 16:53.460
Commander-in-Chief.

298
16:53.460 --> 16:54.360
Comrade Bocheng.

299
16:54.360 --> 16:56.030
Please have a seat.

300
16:56.910 --> 16:59.310
The Military Commission's orders are crystal clear.

301
16:59.310 --> 17:00.620
This is an urgent matter.

302
17:00.620 --> 17:02.350
I'll ask you just one question:

303
17:02.700 --> 17:04.300
when will the troops set out?

304
17:08.220 --> 17:10.280
No matter how urgent an operation is,

305
17:11.670 --> 17:13.349
we still need to assemble the troops.

306
17:13.349 --> 17:13.980
Besides,

307
17:14.390 --> 17:16.430
we need to gather food

308
17:16.589 --> 17:17.480
and other supplies.

309
17:17.480 --> 17:18.609
That all takes time.

310
17:19.140 --> 17:19.829
Also,

311
17:20.220 --> 17:23.020
our Left Route Army has 20 regiments.

312
17:23.500 --> 17:25.230
Unlike the First Front Army...

313
17:26.589 --> 17:27.540
I'm not comparing them,

314
17:27.540 --> 17:28.950
I'm just giving an example.

315
17:28.950 --> 17:30.950
If I had only five or ten men with me,

316
17:31.150 --> 17:32.550
I could cough in a room,

317
17:32.580 --> 17:33.930
and they'd all be standing

318
17:33.930 --> 17:35.660
in the courtyard immediately.

319
17:35.670 --> 17:37.560
Is that what you call assembling the troops?

320
17:37.560 --> 17:38.490
Comrade Guotao,

321
17:38.980 --> 17:40.630
you're going too far with that remark.

322
17:40.630 --> 17:41.560
What do you mean?

323
17:42.670 --> 17:43.540
The wording may be blunt, but the point stands.

324
17:43.540 --> 17:45.070
I'm just giving an example.

325
17:45.150 --> 17:46.080
Comrade Guotao,

326
17:46.160 --> 17:47.090
I take no offense

327
17:47.630 --> 17:49.460
at what you just said.

328
17:50.260 --> 17:51.270
The Right Route Army

329
17:51.270 --> 17:53.630
still includes two corps from the 4th Front Army.

330
17:53.630 --> 17:54.980
Xiangqian and Changhao

331
17:55.360 --> 17:57.330
agree with the Military Commission's orders.

332
17:57.330 --> 17:58.330
I must remind you:

333
17:58.600 --> 17:59.390
we lost the chance

334
17:59.390 --> 18:00.830
to advance north

335
18:01.110 --> 18:02.260
through Songpan

336
18:02.870 --> 18:04.330
because the 4th Front Army

337
18:04.460 --> 18:05.950
dragged its feet.

338
18:06.460 --> 18:07.750
Now, with a formidable enemy before us,

339
18:07.750 --> 18:09.390
if you let another opportunity slip,

340
18:09.390 --> 18:10.990
you'll make a grave mistake.

341
18:17.260 --> 18:18.590
Military opportunity?

342
18:20.260 --> 18:22.750
Do you think heading north is the only opportunity?

343
18:22.750 --> 18:24.870
The Central Committee wants us to go north.

344
18:24.870 --> 18:27.470
If you don't go north, where else are you going?

345
18:28.220 --> 18:29.420
Let me put it this way.

346
18:30.500 --> 18:33.240
I have already called a meeting of the 4th Front Army's

347
18:33.240 --> 18:35.200
cadres at corps level and above.

348
18:35.700 --> 18:37.190
The meeting unanimously agreed that

349
18:37.190 --> 18:39.300
we would head west to Aba

350
18:39.460 --> 18:41.060
and advance toward Qinghai.

351
18:42.830 --> 18:44.760
This is the telegram I just drafted

352
18:44.830 --> 18:48.570
to the Central Committee and the Central Revolutionary Military Commission.

353
18:48.570 --> 18:50.290
Please take a look.

354
18:51.980 --> 18:53.300
If there are no problems,

355
18:53.300 --> 18:54.260
please sign it.

356
18:57.590 --> 18:58.520
Comrade Guotao.

357
18:59.630 --> 19:01.500
How can you go back on your word?

358
19:02.220 --> 19:03.620
You can't put it that way.

359
19:03.910 --> 19:05.430
Wasn't the Military Commission's original plan

360
19:05.430 --> 19:07.830
for the Left Route Army to march west to Aba?

361
19:08.150 --> 19:09.410
I'm simply carrying out

362
19:09.410 --> 19:10.490
the original plan.

363
19:10.740 --> 19:11.910
But the enemy situation

364
19:11.910 --> 19:13.430
has changed drastically now!

365
19:13.430 --> 19:15.630
If the Left Route Army heads west to Aba,

366
19:15.670 --> 19:17.740
it may lose the chance to move north,

367
19:17.950 --> 19:21.350
jeopardizing the Right Route Army's own northward advance.

368
19:21.690 --> 19:23.170
Didn't I just tell you?

369
19:23.350 --> 19:25.460
We can advance toward Qinghai first.

370
19:25.830 --> 19:27.230
If that doesn't work out,

371
19:27.350 --> 19:28.950
we can still continue south.

372
19:29.830 --> 19:32.350
If the Right Route Army can't advance north on its own,

373
19:32.350 --> 19:33.740
it can turn back,

374
19:33.910 --> 19:35.390
attack Fubian and Lifan,

375
19:35.980 --> 19:37.390
and then join us.

376
19:37.540 --> 19:38.300
If we do that,

377
19:38.540 --> 19:40.190
that would leave us completely

378
19:40.190 --> 19:41.300
on the defensive

379
19:41.890 --> 19:44.370
and waste all our previous efforts!

380
19:44.700 --> 19:45.950
Can the decisions of the Central Committee

381
19:45.950 --> 19:47.300
simply be ignored?

382
19:47.670 --> 19:51.300
When a general is in the field, he may disregard orders from the capital.

383
19:51.300 --> 19:52.950
This is also a last resort.

384
19:53.560 --> 19:54.690
In the Party's army,

385
19:55.980 --> 19:57.040
who is the general,

386
19:57.050 --> 19:58.190
and who gives the orders?

387
19:58.190 --> 19:58.870
Good.

388
20:00.060 --> 20:01.190
The Commander-in-Chief is right.

389
20:01.190 --> 20:02.350
Absolutely right.

390
20:02.590 --> 20:06.150
The Party's army must also adhere to organizational principles.

391
20:06.150 --> 20:07.540
I'm the Chief Political Commissar of the Red Army.

392
20:07.540 --> 20:09.060
Under the Party's organizational rules,

393
20:09.060 --> 20:11.060
I have the final say over

394
20:11.430 --> 20:13.070
the Red Army's military operations.

395
20:13.070 --> 20:13.590
No,

396
20:14.110 --> 20:16.020
I'm the Chairman of the Military Commission.

397
20:16.020 --> 20:18.240
The CPC Central Committee has entrusted

398
20:18.240 --> 20:21.060
Comrade Enlai with making the final military decisions.

399
20:21.060 --> 20:22.110
Neither of us

400
20:22.460 --> 20:24.190
can overrule the CPC Central Committee.

401
20:24.190 --> 20:25.700
We all have to listen to the CPC Central Committee.

402
20:25.700 --> 20:26.350
No.

403
20:26.700 --> 20:28.560
The General Political Commissar

404
20:28.850 --> 20:31.710
has the final say on specific military operations.

405
20:32.540 --> 20:35.340
The 4th Front Army has tens of thousands of troops.

406
20:36.070 --> 20:38.070
Do you think anyone can command them

407
20:39.700 --> 20:40.950
without my orders?

408
20:48.460 --> 20:49.390
Comrade Guotao,

409
20:50.780 --> 20:52.740
I firmly oppose your behavior

410
20:57.570 --> 20:59.370
and refuse to sign the telegram.

411
21:19.070 --> 21:20.470
Commander-in-Chief Zhu

412
21:22.200 --> 21:23.770
is still so stubborn.

413
21:34.980 --> 21:36.040
It doesn't matter.

414
21:41.430 --> 21:43.490
Actually, you've already signed it.

415
21:53.500 --> 21:54.630
Reporting for duty!

416
21:54.870 --> 21:56.370
Yang Chengwu reporting for duty.

417
21:56.370 --> 21:57.430
You're here, Comrade Chengwu.

418
21:57.430 --> 21:58.740
Come here. Sit down.

419
22:02.610 --> 22:04.910
[Yang Chengwu, Political Commissar of the 4th Regiment]

420
22:03.110 --> 22:04.110
Comrade Chengwu,

421
22:04.460 --> 22:06.020
you received your orders, right?

422
22:06.020 --> 22:06.910
Yes, I did.

423
22:09.430 --> 22:13.500
The 4th Regiment is the vanguard of the 1st Army,

424
22:13.670 --> 22:17.220
and of the Central Committee and the Military Commission.

425
22:17.950 --> 22:19.170
I called you here to see

426
22:19.170 --> 22:22.020
how your preparations are going.

427
22:23.040 --> 22:24.640
Are there any difficulties?

428
22:26.150 --> 22:28.480
The biggest difficulty right now is food.

429
22:28.500 --> 22:30.260
There's very little grain here.

430
22:30.260 --> 22:31.540
We've tried every way we can,

431
22:31.540 --> 22:33.740
but we've still gathered little grain.

432
22:34.000 --> 22:36.000
Another issue is finding guides.

433
22:36.630 --> 22:37.980
The locals all say

434
22:37.980 --> 22:39.040
the grasslands are a dead zone.

435
22:39.040 --> 22:40.360
Once you go in, you can't come out.

436
22:40.360 --> 22:43.220
We searched for a long time and only found one guide.

437
22:46.170 --> 22:47.210
Comrade Chengwu.

438
22:48.220 --> 22:49.700
The two problems you've mentioned

439
22:49.700 --> 22:51.630
are both objective difficulties,

440
22:52.430 --> 22:54.290
especially the shortage of food.

441
22:54.390 --> 22:57.420
I believe every unit

442
22:57.630 --> 22:59.290
is facing the same challenge.

443
22:59.980 --> 23:01.590
When faced with objective difficulties,

444
23:01.590 --> 23:02.590
all we can do is

445
23:03.910 --> 23:05.880
try our best to overcome them.

446
23:06.740 --> 23:07.500
Besides,

447
23:07.780 --> 23:09.980
to cross the grasslands successfully,

448
23:10.150 --> 23:12.430
we must overcome not only objective difficulties

449
23:12.430 --> 23:14.290
but also those within ourselves.

450
23:14.980 --> 23:15.670
First,

451
23:15.950 --> 23:19.320
we must overcome our fear of crossing the grasslands.

452
23:20.060 --> 23:20.780
Second,

453
23:20.910 --> 23:22.960
we must make the whole army understand

454
23:22.960 --> 23:24.980
the importance of crossing the grasslands

455
23:24.980 --> 23:26.350
and continuing north.

456
23:26.590 --> 23:28.190
Why are we crossing the grasslands?

457
23:28.190 --> 23:29.590
What will we achieve once we cross them?

458
23:29.590 --> 23:30.740
This must be made crystal clear.

459
23:30.740 --> 23:32.020
Once you make this clear,

460
23:32.020 --> 23:33.740
the soldiers will once again show the same courage they did

461
23:33.740 --> 23:35.110
when they captured Luding Bridge,

462
23:35.110 --> 23:37.170
and press on to complete the mission.

463
23:37.390 --> 23:38.740
Rest assured, Chairman.

464
23:38.740 --> 23:40.870
I'll return, convey your instructions

465
23:40.870 --> 23:42.200
to the entire regiment,

466
23:42.300 --> 23:43.780
rally everyone, and step up

467
23:43.780 --> 23:45.190
our efforts to complete this mission.

468
23:45.190 --> 23:45.780
Good.

469
23:46.460 --> 23:48.460
Boosting morale is very important.

470
23:48.640 --> 23:49.200
Understood.

471
23:49.200 --> 23:50.300
Reporting for duty!

472
23:50.300 --> 23:50.870
Chairman Mao.

473
23:50.870 --> 23:54.000
Comrade Luofu asks you to attend a meeting immediately.

474
23:54.700 --> 23:56.560
Chairman, you haven't eaten yet.

475
23:57.220 --> 23:59.080
Comrade Chengwu, have you eaten?

476
23:59.350 --> 24:00.220
I haven't eaten.

477
24:00.220 --> 24:00.930
Then sit down

478
24:00.930 --> 24:01.950
and eat right here.

479
24:01.950 --> 24:02.780
I'll just go back and eat, Chairman.

480
24:02.780 --> 24:03.240
Come on.

481
24:03.300 --> 24:03.900
Chairman.

482
24:04.190 --> 24:05.020
Just eat here.

483
24:05.390 --> 24:06.430
Give him my meal.

484
24:06.630 --> 24:07.630
Keep an eye on him.

485
24:07.630 --> 24:09.490
Don't let him go until he finishes

486
24:19.150 --> 24:21.350
Political Commissar Yang, please eat.

487
24:22.540 --> 24:23.800
It's highland barley.

488
25:00.690 --> 25:02.410
Eat slowly. Don't choke.

489
25:02.850 --> 25:03.680
Thank you.

490
25:26.590 --> 25:29.250
There's little water left, so use it sparingly.

491
25:35.750 --> 25:38.030
Comrade, is something wrong?

492
25:39.390 --> 25:41.220
Nothing. Go ahead and eat.

493
25:45.740 --> 25:47.400
How many meals do you eat a day?

494
25:48.430 --> 25:49.220
Two.

495
25:50.110 --> 25:52.310
Do you get this much to eat at every meal?

496
25:52.980 --> 25:55.710
We don't even eat as well as the men in the Company.

497
25:55.740 --> 25:57.500
Those six small flatbreads you're eating

498
25:57.500 --> 25:59.700
are the Chairman's ration for two days.

499
26:24.430 --> 26:25.560
Thank you, Comrade.

500
26:25.980 --> 26:26.900
I'm full.

501
26:28.050 --> 26:31.060
The Chairman said you have to finish your meal before leaving.

502
26:31.060 --> 26:31.780
I'm full.

503
26:32.400 --> 26:34.060
Please tell the Chairman that

504
26:34.060 --> 26:36.660
the 4th Red Regiment will fulfill its mission.

505
26:56.800 --> 26:59.120
H-He is simply out of his mind!

506
26:59.300 --> 27:00.110
Zhang Guotao

507
27:00.300 --> 27:01.980
has no organizational discipline at all!

508
27:01.980 --> 27:02.780
He changes his mind just like that!

509
27:02.780 --> 27:03.710
Comrade Zedong.

510
27:06.190 --> 27:07.430
Zhang Guotao has changed his mind again?

511
27:07.430 --> 27:08.230
That's right.

512
27:08.350 --> 27:09.350
He sent a telegram

513
27:09.540 --> 27:10.500
refusing to march north and

514
27:10.500 --> 27:12.510
insisting on heading west toward Aba.

515
27:12.510 --> 27:15.700
Zhang Guotao is using his troops to act independently,

516
27:16.540 --> 27:18.060
openly defying the Central Committee!

517
27:18.060 --> 27:18.780
I suggest we

518
27:18.950 --> 27:20.910
convene an enlarged Politburo meeting,

519
27:20.910 --> 27:22.150
openly and firmly opposing

520
27:22.150 --> 27:23.950
Zhang Guotao's erroneous line.

521
27:27.780 --> 27:28.700
That's inappropriate.

522
27:28.700 --> 27:29.630
Comrade Zedong.

523
27:29.900 --> 27:32.090
He's going too far.

524
27:32.120 --> 27:34.270
How long do we have to endure this?

525
27:35.500 --> 27:37.700
We endure this not because we fear Zhang Guotao,

526
27:37.700 --> 27:40.240
but for the sake of our overall strategy of marching north.

527
27:40.240 --> 27:42.510
Given our goal of marching north to fight the Japanese army,

528
27:42.510 --> 27:44.230
now is not the time to launch

529
27:44.260 --> 27:45.740
a political struggle against Zhang Guotao.

530
27:45.740 --> 27:46.530
It would also undermine

531
27:46.530 --> 27:48.150
the vital unity we share with our comrades

532
27:48.150 --> 27:49.350
in the 4th Front Army.

533
27:50.220 --> 27:51.150
I think we should

534
27:51.460 --> 27:53.520
hold an enlarged Politburo meeting,

535
27:54.110 --> 27:56.670
but avoid turning it into a struggle over political lines.

536
27:56.670 --> 27:58.070
Let's clarify the military line first

537
27:58.070 --> 28:00.330
like what we did at the Zunyi Conference.

538
28:00.670 --> 28:03.460
We must make sure the Red Army's commanders and soldiers

539
28:03.460 --> 28:04.780
understand why we're marching north.

540
28:04.780 --> 28:06.910
Above all, we must ensure our comrades

541
28:07.060 --> 28:08.630
in the 4th Front Army understand this.

542
28:08.630 --> 28:10.830
I agree with Comrade Zedong's opinion.

543
28:11.300 --> 28:13.350
As Zedong mentioned earlier,

544
28:13.590 --> 28:14.950
in these extraordinary circumstances,

545
28:14.950 --> 28:16.010
we must strengthen

546
28:16.020 --> 28:18.430
the Central Politburo's leadership.

547
28:18.700 --> 28:21.020
We must clearly define each member of the Standing Committee's responsibilities.

548
28:21.020 --> 28:23.110
We should hold a Standing Committee meeting at least once a week.

549
28:23.110 --> 28:25.630
If necessary, we need to convene an interim Standing Committee meeting

550
28:25.630 --> 28:28.300
We must make full use of the Standing Committee's authority.

551
28:28.300 --> 28:28.760
I agree.

552
28:28.950 --> 28:29.700
I agree.

553
28:30.350 --> 28:30.980
I agree.

554
28:31.060 --> 28:31.540
Good.

555
28:32.150 --> 28:34.350
As for the specific division of labor within the Standing Committee,

556
28:34.350 --> 28:35.300
here is my proposal:

557
28:35.300 --> 28:37.300
I will take charge of organizational work,

558
28:37.300 --> 28:40.060
and Comrade Li Weihan can assist me.

559
28:40.200 --> 28:42.680
Comrade Bo Gu will be responsible for publicity campaign.

560
28:42.680 --> 28:45.240
Comrade Jiaxiang will be in charge of the Political Department,

561
28:45.240 --> 28:48.500
while Comrade Kai Feng will oversee the Ethnic Committee.

562
28:48.500 --> 28:50.360
I propose that Comrade Mao Zedong

563
28:50.830 --> 28:51.930
assume full responsibility

564
28:51.930 --> 28:54.820
for military affairs while Comrade Enlai is ill.

565
28:55.060 --> 28:55.560
I agree.

566
28:55.700 --> 28:56.300
I agree.

567
28:56.810 --> 28:57.600
I agree.

568
29:01.520 --> 29:05.000
[Deng Yingchao, Committee Member of the Party General Branch of the Cadre Rest-and-Rehabilitation Company]

569
29:26.780 --> 29:27.430
Enlai.

570
29:30.740 --> 29:33.600
Chairman Mao sent me to look after you.

571
29:49.510 --> 29:50.840
Are you feeling better?

572
29:51.630 --> 29:52.670
I'm fine.

573
30:07.110 --> 30:08.170
Comrade Yingchao.

574
30:08.250 --> 30:09.050
Chairman Mao.

575
30:09.090 --> 30:10.490
How are you doing, Enlai?

576
30:10.880 --> 30:11.600
I'm fine.

577
30:12.530 --> 30:13.390
How are you doing, Yingchao?

578
30:13.390 --> 30:13.980
I'm fine.

579
30:15.080 --> 30:16.540
I'll leave you two to talk.

580
30:35.940 --> 30:37.070
As things stand now,

581
30:37.720 --> 30:40.640
the Left Route Army won't be able

582
30:41.580 --> 30:43.180
to march north anytime soon.

583
30:44.300 --> 30:45.190
Our plan is

584
30:45.770 --> 30:47.100
for the Right Route Army

585
30:47.500 --> 30:48.950
to cross the grasslands first,

586
30:48.950 --> 30:50.060
while we

587
30:51.220 --> 30:52.680
keep urging them forward.

588
30:54.020 --> 30:54.870
I...

589
30:56.460 --> 30:57.700
completely agree

590
30:58.500 --> 31:01.430
with the Politburo Standing Committee's decision.

591
31:01.700 --> 31:05.190
My only concern is for

592
31:05.780 --> 31:07.380
Comrades Zhu De and Bocheng.

593
31:08.260 --> 31:09.430
I heard Zhang Guotao

594
31:12.390 --> 31:16.780
had imprisoned Zeng Zhongsheng,

595
31:17.630 --> 31:20.740
former secretary of the Sichuan-Shaanxi Provincial Committee

596
31:20.740 --> 31:22.980
and brother of Comrade Zeng Xisheng

597
31:24.040 --> 31:25.950
of the Military Commission's 2nd Bureau,

598
31:25.950 --> 31:27.500
simply for opposing him.

599
31:28.670 --> 31:31.990
They say that after a mysterious fire

600
31:32.300 --> 31:35.830
broke out in Zhuokeji the day before yesterday,

601
31:36.500 --> 31:39.220
Zeng Zhongsheng disappeared.

602
31:40.980 --> 31:42.600
I am deeply worried.

603
31:48.480 --> 31:49.090
Enlai,

604
31:51.060 --> 31:53.060
I share your concerns.

605
31:53.300 --> 31:56.150
I've discussed them with the other comrades as well.

606
31:56.150 --> 31:57.220
At a time like this,

607
31:57.900 --> 32:00.180
recalling Zhu De and the others

608
32:00.800 --> 32:02.530
is clearly out of the question.

609
32:04.670 --> 32:06.110
But I believe one thing.

610
32:06.700 --> 32:07.850
The Commander-in-Chief is

611
32:07.850 --> 32:11.240
one of the founders of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army.

612
32:11.240 --> 32:13.840
He is known abroad as the Father of the Red Army.

613
32:14.190 --> 32:16.010
If Zhang Guotao were to

614
32:16.040 --> 32:17.770
harm Commander-in-Chief Zhu,

615
32:17.870 --> 32:19.630
he'd be openly turning

616
32:19.650 --> 32:20.860
against the Red Army.

617
32:21.590 --> 32:24.250
I don't think Zhang Guotao would dare to do that.

618
32:29.500 --> 32:32.870
Has the Right Route Army's plan

619
32:32.890 --> 32:34.190
to cross the grasslands been finalized?

620
32:34.190 --> 32:36.830
We'll cross the grasslands along two routes.

621
32:37.500 --> 32:38.630
One route,

622
32:39.580 --> 32:41.890
Xu Xiangqian and Chen Changhao

623
32:41.920 --> 32:43.950
will lead the 4th and 30th Red Army Corps

624
32:43.950 --> 32:47.110
into the grasslands through Dongya and Lazi Mountain.

625
32:47.700 --> 32:50.060
Jianying and Cheng Shicai

626
32:50.640 --> 32:52.470
will lead three regiments as the vanguard.

627
32:52.470 --> 32:54.210
The other route will take the 1st Red Army

628
32:54.210 --> 32:57.730
from Mao'ergai into the grasslands through Quding Bridge,

629
32:58.130 --> 33:00.220
with the 4th Red Regiment serving as the vanguard.

630
33:00.220 --> 33:02.500
The Central Committee's headquarters and the Red Army University

631
33:02.500 --> 33:03.960
will move with the 1st Red Army.

632
33:03.960 --> 33:07.160
Peng Dehuai will lead the 3rd Red Army to bring up the rear.

633
33:09.110 --> 33:10.060
Comrade Zedong.

634
33:12.150 --> 33:15.110
I have a request.

635
33:15.390 --> 33:16.020
Go ahead.

636
33:16.980 --> 33:20.460
Please convey it to the Central Committee on my behalf.

637
33:24.940 --> 33:26.050
Don't move.

638
33:27.950 --> 33:28.630
Go ahead.

639
33:30.350 --> 33:34.430
My condition is very serious now.

640
33:35.590 --> 33:39.260
Not only can I not continue to work for the Party,

641
33:40.830 --> 33:45.220
I'm afraid I won't be able to cross the grasslands either.

642
33:46.850 --> 33:48.680
I'll only be a burden

643
33:49.510 --> 33:51.620
to the other comrades.

644
33:54.110 --> 33:55.870
I only ask that...

645
33:59.950 --> 34:00.880
Absolutely not.

646
34:01.220 --> 34:03.660
The Red Army needs you, Zhou Enlai,

647
34:04.330 --> 34:06.060
and so does the Party.

648
34:06.810 --> 34:07.810
Rest and recover.

649
34:08.350 --> 34:09.550
You said it yourself:

650
34:09.790 --> 34:11.580
we must stand united for the Party.

651
34:11.580 --> 34:13.040
For the cause of the Party,

652
34:13.340 --> 34:15.330
you must endure the pain.

653
34:17.060 --> 34:18.179
Comrade Zedong?

654
34:22.270 --> 34:23.060
Enlai.

655
34:23.750 --> 34:25.010
Before the Long March,

656
34:25.500 --> 34:27.659
I fell ill in Yudu.

657
34:28.020 --> 34:29.100
I know...

658
34:29.120 --> 34:31.520
I wasn't originally on the transfer list.

659
34:31.620 --> 34:32.489
You insisted

660
34:33.350 --> 34:34.880
that I should come with you.

661
34:36.179 --> 34:37.070
That's how

662
34:39.270 --> 34:40.870
I came to join the Long March.

663
34:41.139 --> 34:42.540
Now I want to tell you:

664
34:43.060 --> 34:44.389
no matter what it takes,

665
34:44.909 --> 34:46.239
I'll carry you on my back

666
34:46.620 --> 34:48.659
or get you a stretcher—

667
34:49.100 --> 34:52.020
I'll definitely take you across the grasslands.

668
34:52.389 --> 34:53.449
Do you understand?

669
34:53.920 --> 34:56.360
We'll do this together.

670
35:31.180 --> 35:32.020
Xiaochao.

671
35:35.500 --> 35:37.310
While you were talking,

672
35:38.010 --> 35:39.820
I picked more than 170 lice

673
35:39.910 --> 35:42.020
off your vest.

674
36:08.390 --> 36:10.710
On August 20, 1935,

675
36:11.550 --> 36:13.160
the CPC Central Committee

676
36:13.180 --> 36:15.380
held an enlarged meeting at Mao'ergai.

677
36:16.310 --> 36:18.020
At the meeting, Mao Zedong gave a clear,

678
36:18.020 --> 36:21.100
detailed military analysis of the two possible routes:

679
36:21.100 --> 36:22.430
marching north into Shaanxi and Gansu

680
36:22.430 --> 36:23.100
and moving west into

681
36:23.100 --> 36:23.870
Qinghai, Ningxia,

682
36:23.870 --> 36:24.980
and Xinjiang.

683
36:25.430 --> 36:28.580
He asserted that heading north meant shifting to the counteroffensive

684
36:28.580 --> 36:30.550
and entering a new phase of the revolution,

685
36:30.550 --> 36:34.880
while going west would be a retreat on both the military and political fronts.

686
36:36.190 --> 36:38.140
The attendees, including cadres from

687
36:38.140 --> 36:40.230
the 4th Front Army,

688
36:40.230 --> 36:42.230
agreed with Mao Zedong's proposal.

689
36:42.430 --> 36:44.060
The meeting's conclusions were eventually

690
36:44.060 --> 36:45.870
incorporated into the "Supplementary Decision

691
36:45.870 --> 36:47.600
on Current Strategic Policy,"

692
36:47.710 --> 36:51.620
which was circulated through the Red Army, including the Left Route Army.

693
36:51.620 --> 36:53.020
The Mao'ergai Conference

694
36:53.020 --> 36:54.750
reaffirmed the Red Army's strategy of moving north

695
36:54.750 --> 36:57.370
to establish a base in Shaanxi and Gansu.

696
36:57.810 --> 36:59.360
It also revised the specific deployment

697
36:59.360 --> 37:02.280
outlined in the "Xia-Tao Campaign Plan"

698
37:02.580 --> 37:04.980
and was of great historical significance.

699
37:17.420 --> 37:18.100
Report!

700
37:18.170 --> 37:19.810
Vice Chairman Zhou is dying!

701
37:32.340 --> 37:33.060
Enlai.

702
37:33.970 --> 37:34.820
Enlai.

703
37:37.390 --> 37:38.550
Enlai, wake up.

704
37:39.020 --> 37:39.660
Enlai.

705
37:40.510 --> 37:41.640
Vice Chairman Zhou.

706
37:42.570 --> 37:43.370
Enlai.

707
37:43.980 --> 37:44.830
Enlai.

708
37:47.370 --> 37:48.370
Comrade Wang Bin.

709
37:48.800 --> 37:49.910
Wake up.

710
37:52.520 --> 37:53.650
Comrade Wang Bin.

711
37:54.790 --> 37:56.980
Comrade Wang Bin, hurry up.

712
37:56.980 --> 37:57.790
Don't rush me!

713
37:57.790 --> 37:59.830
I can't diagnose him just by looking at him, right?

714
37:59.830 --> 38:01.140
He's unconscious in there!

715
38:01.140 --> 38:02.750
Can't you think of something else?

716
38:02.750 --> 38:03.340
Chen Geng.

717
38:03.340 --> 38:03.880
Enlai.

718
38:03.910 --> 38:04.970
How is Enlai doing?

719
38:05.100 --> 38:06.630
He's unconscious in there.

720
38:07.140 --> 38:07.750
How is he?

721
38:11.660 --> 38:12.450
Chairman!

722
38:12.910 --> 38:14.460
He said his stomach hurt,

723
38:14.640 --> 38:17.720
then passed a basinful of mucus, pus, and blood.

724
38:17.870 --> 38:20.470
Then he lost consciousness and developed a high fever.

725
38:20.470 --> 38:21.880
He hasn't woken up since.

726
38:21.910 --> 38:22.950
What should we do?

727
38:23.090 --> 38:24.290
I've found the cause.

728
38:25.710 --> 38:27.500
In Vice Chairman Zhou's stool,

729
38:27.160 --> 38:28.740
[Wang Bin, Health Physician for Central Leaders of the Red Army]

730
38:27.540 --> 38:29.270
I found a large number of amoebas.

731
38:29.270 --> 38:31.460
Combined with the enlarged liver and his yellowish-green complexion...

732
38:31.460 --> 38:32.500
Just give me the conclusion!

733
38:32.500 --> 38:33.430
It appears to be

734
38:33.430 --> 38:34.750
an amoebic liver abscess.

735
38:34.750 --> 38:36.390
Just tell us if you can treat it or not!

736
38:36.390 --> 38:37.390
The emetine I brought from Zunyi

737
38:37.390 --> 38:38.500
is a specific treatment

738
38:38.500 --> 38:40.270
for amoebic infection.

739
38:40.390 --> 38:42.310
But Vice Chairman Zhou's symptoms are quite severe.

740
38:42.310 --> 38:44.460
If the infection continues to spread to the abdomen and chest,

741
38:44.460 --> 38:45.630
his life will be in danger.

742
38:45.630 --> 38:46.580
You...

743
38:46.830 --> 38:48.350
Comrade Wang Bin!

744
38:48.350 --> 38:49.910
Just tell us what to do

745
38:49.910 --> 38:51.180
to stop it from spreading!

746
38:51.180 --> 38:51.830
Ice cubes.

747
38:51.920 --> 38:52.870
We can use ice to cool him down.

748
38:52.870 --> 38:53.950
Find some ice!

749
38:54.140 --> 38:55.950
Hold on. Where can we find ice now?

750
38:55.950 --> 38:57.140
We might find some at night,

751
38:57.140 --> 38:58.670
but it melts during the day.

752
39:00.660 --> 39:02.580
Guards, come with me!

753
39:06.330 --> 39:07.330
What should we do?

754
39:24.540 --> 39:25.560
Emetine injection.

755
39:25.560 --> 39:26.690
Come on. Hurry.

756
39:28.500 --> 39:29.270
Help me out.

757
39:32.100 --> 39:33.870
Are you sure this medicine will work?

758
39:33.870 --> 39:34.790
It's a specific treatment,

759
39:34.790 --> 39:35.910
but we can only try it.

760
39:35.910 --> 39:37.490
So you're saying there's no guarantee?

761
39:37.490 --> 39:38.700
He's still in danger?

762
39:38.730 --> 39:40.020
Chairman, don't worry.

763
39:40.020 --> 39:41.310
If we can find ice,

764
39:41.310 --> 39:42.410
it may help reduce the inflammation.

765
39:42.410 --> 39:43.940
Give him the injection now!

766
40:06.500 --> 40:07.100
Dismount.

767
40:12.950 --> 40:13.930
Regiment Commander!

768
40:13.930 --> 40:15.660
I'm fine, Regiment Commander.

769
40:16.130 --> 40:16.700
Let's go.

770
40:19.650 --> 40:21.450
Regiment Commander, slow down.

771
40:35.040 --> 40:35.770
Careful.

772
40:41.960 --> 40:42.600
Come on.

773
40:44.110 --> 40:45.370
Climb a little higher.

774
40:45.760 --> 40:47.030
There's ice up there.

775
40:49.530 --> 40:50.730
Regiment Commander.

776
40:50.790 --> 40:51.500
We found it!

777
40:51.910 --> 40:53.180
Ice, ice.

778
40:54.320 --> 40:55.580
Come on, get the tools.

779
41:03.810 --> 41:04.410
Pack it up.

780
41:06.040 --> 41:06.690
Here.

781
41:07.340 --> 41:08.270
Keep packing it.

782
41:20.580 --> 41:21.140
More.

783
41:27.350 --> 41:28.800
Take as much as we can.

784
41:29.720 --> 41:30.280
Yes, sir!

785
41:37.430 --> 41:38.230
Keep packing!

786
41:40.130 --> 41:40.860
Pack in more.

787
41:48.810 --> 41:50.010
Regiment Commander.

788
41:50.390 --> 41:51.370
Why are you taking off your clothes?

789
41:51.370 --> 41:54.250
Use my clothes to wrap the larger chunks.

790
41:59.250 --> 42:00.380
It's a long journey.

791
42:00.850 --> 42:02.450
The ice will melt otherwise.

792
42:03.110 --> 42:03.710
All right.

793
42:04.170 --> 42:06.400
Let's go when we're done packing.

794
42:06.560 --> 42:08.560
Okay, let's go. It's all wrapped up.

795
42:13.300 --> 42:16.890
-Regiment Commander! -Regiment Commander!

796
42:27.230 --> 42:27.760
Let's go.

797
42:50.130 --> 42:51.190
Is that enough ice?

798
42:51.950 --> 42:52.870
Is it enough?

799
42:54.170 --> 42:55.500
If not, I'll go get more.

800
42:56.080 --> 42:56.870
Here.
